{"name":"Prize Winning Orchid","hex":"#cc9dc6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"prize","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["That which is taken from another; something captured; a thing seized by force, stratagem, or superior power.","Anything captured by a belligerent using the rights of war; especially, property captured at sea in virtue of the rights of war, as a vessel."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To consider highly valuable; to esteem.","To set or estimate the value of; to appraise; to price; to rate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prize"},{"term":"winning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of win"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That constitutes a win.","That leads to success."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winning"},{"term":"orchid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the orchid family (Orchidaceae), bearing unusually-shaped flowers of beautiful colours. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A light bluish-red, violet-red or purple colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a light purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prize","blocks":[{"text":"A prize is an award to be given to a person or a group of people to recognize and reward their actions and achievements. Official prizes often involve monetary rewards as well as the fame that comes with them. Some prizes are also associated with extravagant awarding ceremonies, such as the Academy Awards."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Mall_culture_jakarta59.jpg/330px-Mall_culture_jakarta59.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prize","wikidata":"Q5257307"},{"title":"Orchid","blocks":[{"text":"Orchids are plants that belong to the family Orchidaceae, a diverse and widespread group of flowering plants with blooms that are often colourful and fragrant. Orchids are cosmopolitan plants, living in diverse habitats on every continent except Antarctica. The world's richest diversity of orchid genera and species is in the tropics. Many species are epiphytes, living on trees. The flowers and their pollination mechanisms are highly specialized, attracting insect pollinators by colour, pattern, scent, pheromones, and sometimes by mimicking female insects. Orchids have very small seeds, relying on fungal partners for germination. Some orchids have no leaves, either photosynthesizing with their roots or relying entirely on fungal partners for food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid","wikidata":"Q25308"},{"title":"Orchid (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Orchid is a bright rich purple color that resembles the color which various orchids often exhibit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Labiata.jpg/330px-Labiata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid_(color)","wikidata":"Q1925148"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Skate_Contest_Prize_Skate4Changes.jpg/500px-Skate_Contest_Prize_Skate4Changes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Skate_Contest_Prize_Skate4Changes.jpg/1280px-Skate_Contest_Prize_Skate4Changes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Skate_Contest_Prize_Skate4Changes.jpg/500px-Skate_Contest_Prize_Skate4Changes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.